y","statements":["LogBrunnMinkowski"]}],"scope":"The logarithmic Brunn–Minkowski conjecture asserts that logarithmic interpolation of origin-symmetric convex bodies preserves the geometric-mean lower bound for volume. The formalized result proves, for every dimension $n\\ge1$, such bodies $K,L\\subset\\mathbb R^n$, and $0\\le t\\le1$, that their logarithmic Wulff combination has volume at least $|K|^{1-t}|L|^t$. It assumes neither boundary smoothness nor coordinatewise unconditionality.","title":"Logarithmic and <i>L</i><sub><i>p</i></sub> Brunn–Minkowski inequalities and the B-conjecture","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/docs/091.md"}},"provenance":{"kind":"computed-navigation","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","rule":"Projection of the pinned ledger; no new mathematical assessment."},"reader_comparison":{"headline_coverage":"agree","method":"Compare reported scope categories; notes remain attributed and are not adjudicated.","points":[{"definitions_to_check":null,"gap":"The B-conjecture for every even log-concave Radon measure (the abstract derives it via Saroglou's transfer theorem and a support-subspace reduction) and the L_p Brunn–Minkowski inequality for 0 < p < 1 (derivable from log-BM by a classical argument) are not stated.","note":null,"reading":"reading:3f90449f41750395a7b9468e","source_term":"NARROWER — UNDECLARED","state":"narrower"},{"definitions_to_check":"`wulff f := {x | ∀ u, ‖u‖ = 1 → ⟪x, u⟫ ≤ f u}` and `support K u := sSup (image of ⟪·,u⟫ on K)` define the log combination by hand (standard Wulff-shape definition); ENNReal `^` with real exponent `1 - t` on volumes","gap":null,"note":"Only the Lebesgue-volume log-Brunn-Minkowski inequality; the scalar-dilation B-conjecture for even log-concave measures and the L_p Brunn-Minkowski inequality for 0<p<1 are not stated.","reading":"reading:a124ad0194a744208ad622ee","source_term":"partial"